  "body": "Google sign-in previously selected existing credentials by email, which cannot establish identity when addresses are shared or imported. This change binds the verified Google issuer and exact subject to a credential, requires current account credentials for explicit linking, and requires a separate `createNewAccount` signal plus terms for new signup. Legacy consent-only clients cannot create an empty duplicate account. Web and mobile expose the linking choice without transferring roles, passwords, ownership, or consent.\n\nContact creation in bookings, companies, leads, and the retained Records form uses actor-scoped request keys across failed responses and field edits. Closing or completing a form ends that attempt. Shared emails/names remain valid for distinct people. The Live Session multi-step change was removed from this PR; its atomic backend/frontend follow-up is being implemented separately.\n\nMigration 108 adds scoped provider bindings without inferring or backfilling existing identities. Its introduction commit is verified in this branch ancestry. The first 107 manifest entries are preserved. Schema rollback refuses to destroy established bindings.\n\nValidation: 108 migration applications, repeat execution, and full schema verification passed against an isolated restored production database, with zero inferred bindings. PostgreSQL authentication tests cover conflicts, disabled credentials, shared email, concurrency, retries and rollback. Latest local web login tests (10), contact retry tests (5), mobile authentication tests (32), web/mobile TypeScript, and mobile lint passed. Required CI runs on the exact head; an earlier WebKit recovery-dialog failure remains tracked until the fresh browser job passes. Local recovery repetitions produced two passes and one resource-sensitive timeout, not a clean result.\n\nMobile companions: diegueins680/TDF-mobile#97 and #99 are merged; root pins the published #99 source commit. Physical iOS Google sign-in remains an explicit native production-release gate; no attached physical device was available, so this PR does not claim native publication.\n\nCore cleanup is already deployed via #426 at a81e48ea9e68b495562ae1f6592654c043dc97eb. Verified production outcome: 241 examined, two safe duplicate groups merged, three records archived, one complementary pair linked, 14 classified groups blocked for authorized conflict resolution, zero failed merge operations. This PR has not yet been deployed.\n",
